English Translation:
## 3. ENGLISH TRANSLATION

### Document 1

**The King**

Since we held imprisoned one Berenguer de Vilaragut for certain very grave crimes touching our person, and this same [man] today, which is Sunday, at vespers has broken [out of] the prison and has fled from it, we tell you and expressly command you, under [pain of] our wrath and indignation, that as soon as [you receive] the present [letters], with supreme diligence you should search for the said Berenguer within the jurisdiction committed to you, both within and without, and [you should] have him [brought to us] dead or captured and send him to us. And furthermore, you should cause to be notified by public proclamation to all the worthy men of your jurisdiction that if they know [the whereabouts of] this same [person], they should denounce [him] to you, and [you should] deliver [any] denunciation to us, so that we may have this same [person] in our hand, as is stated.

Given in Barcelona under our secret seal on the 20th day of July at the hour of prime, in the year of the Nativity of Our Lord 1387, and sealed with our small ring.

**[Addressed]** to the Vicar and Bailiff of Vilafranca del Penedès and their lieutenants.

**[Chancery notation]** The Lord King commanded [this] to me, Bernard de Jonquera.

**[Similes]** Similar letters were sent to those written below under the same date, and were [dispatched]:

First, to the Bailiff of Sitges and of Cuitrude[?] and of Cubells and his lieutenant;
Item, to the Vicar and Bailiff of Manresa and Bages and their lieutenants;
Item, to the Vicar and Bailiff of Vic and Osona and their lieutenants;
Item, to the Vicar and Bailiff of Girona and their lieutenants;
Item, to the Bailiff of Sant Feliu de Guíxols and his lieutenant;
Item, to the Vicar of Tarragona and their lieutenants;
Item, to the Subvicar and Bailiff of Berga and Berguedà and their lieutenants;
Item, to the Bailiff of the town of Arbúcies and his lieutenant.

